---
const mailtoBody = encodeURIComponent(`Product URL:

Flow that breaks:

What users do instead:

What this costs you:

Who needs the review:
`);
---

<section id="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="watermark" aria-hidden="true">GUIDE · SCAFFOLD · CONTINUE</div>

    <div class="fade-up">
      <div class="hero-label">Guidance Failure Architecture</div>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up">
      <h1>Your product is not losing users because the interface is ugly.</h1>
      <p class="hero-subheadline">It is losing them where guidance disappears.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up">
      <p class="hero-summary hero-summary-large">
        I help SaaS and software teams locate the hidden breakdown inside the flow everyone keeps arguing about:
        onboarding that does not activate, intake that returns unusable data, AI flows that increase uncertainty,
        dashboards that inform without guiding, and support-heavy moments the product should have handled earlier.
      </p>
      <p class="authority-line">Not a UI pass. A read of the missing scaffold behind the screen.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up hero-ctas">
      <a href="#contact" class="btn-primary">
        Send the flow that breaks
      </a>
      <a href="#offer" class="btn-outline">
        See what the review includes
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up hero-tags">
      <span class="tag">Guidance failure</span>
      <span class="tag">Hidden scaffold</span>
      <span class="tag">Onboarding</span>
      <span class="tag">Intake</span>
      <span class="tag">AI-assisted flows</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
